<header><p class="st-kicker">other · Anatolia and the Levant</p><h1 class="st-title">Government of the Grand National Assembly</h1><p class="st-meta">1920 CE – 1923 CE · capital Ankara</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The Ankara government of Mustafa Kemal, which won the Turkish War of Independence and replaced the Ottoman Empire with the Turkish Republic.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>After the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/allies">Allies</a> formally occupied <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantinople">Constantinople</a> in March 1920, nationalist deputies and delegates met in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ankara">Ankara</a> and on 23 April 1920 opened the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/grand-national-assembly-of-turkey">Grand National Assembly</a>, which claimed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sovereignty">sovereignty</a> in the name of the nation. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mustafa-kemal-ataturk">Mustafa Kemal</a> was elected its president.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The assembly governed directly through ministers it elected and adopted a constitution in 1921 vesting <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sovereignty">sovereignty</a> in the nation. It rejected the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-sevres">Treaty of Sevres</a>, signed treaties with <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/russian-sfsr">Soviet Russia</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kars">Kars</a>, and secured French withdrawal by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-ankara-1921">Treaty of Ankara</a>. Its army stopped the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greeks">Greeks</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-sakarya">Sakarya</a> in 1921 and drove them out in 1922 under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mustafa-kemal-ataturk">Mustafa Kemal</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ismet-inonu">Ismet</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>The assembly abolished the Ottoman sultanate in November 1922, won recognition in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-lausanne">Treaty of Lausanne</a> of July 1923, and proclaimed the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/republic-of-turkey">Republic of Turkey</a> on 29 October 1923.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/government-of-the-grand-national-assembly.jpg" alt="Government of the Grand National Assembly" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: User:Orwellianist · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_Ottoman_Empire_(1844%E2%80%931922).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1920 CE – 1923 CE</dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>other</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Ankara</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Mustafa Kemal, Ismet Inönü, Fevzi Çakmak</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Turkish</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd>Turkey</dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Ankara Government, Grand National Assembly of Turkey government</dd></dl></aside></div>
